## Why This Is Asked
Gauge ability to design end-to-end CAPA around privilege management, multi-tenant risk, and cross-region controls.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model
- Lifecycle state machine
- Policy-as-code and RBAC for service accounts
- Canary rollout and RCA templates
- Observability across tenants

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal REST handler sketch (Node.js/Express)
app.post('/caps', (req, res) => {
  // create CAPA with linked logs/traces
  res.status(201).send({ id: 'capa_001' });
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle false positives and ensure minimal tenant impact?
- What data retention/privacy considerations apply to CAPA artifacts and logs?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests end-to-end CAPA design with privacy considerations in data-labeling.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model with evidence and lineage
- Cross-tenant lifecycle with SLAs
- API for CAPA creation/update with logs/traces and policy links
- Privacy metrics: exposure window, recurrence rate
- RCA template and canary rollback plan

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal CAPA type
class CAPARecord {
  constructor(id, evidence, lineage, owners) {
    this.id = id; this.evidence = evidence; this.lineage = lineage; this.owners = owners;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you quantify exposure window in MTTI terms?
- What telemetry would you add to prove recurrence reduction after rollout?

## Why This Is Asked

This question tests ability to design a CAPA for ML drift in a real-time system with multi-region considerations, plus practical data modeling and API design.

## Key Concepts

- CAPA data model with evidence and region
- Lifecycle state machine for CAPA progression
- Minimal REST API endpoints for create/update
- Region-aware metrics and canary remediation
- RCA templating for root-cause communication

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal API sketch
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
app.use(express.json());

app.post('/caps', (req, res) => {
  // create CAPA with fields from req.body
  res.status(201).send({ id: 'CAPA-001' });
});
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate canary results before roll-out?
- What data lineage artifacts would you capture and store?
